{"units": [{"id": "de-quote34", "translation": "There is the sea—who will quench it?"}, {"id": "de-quote35", "translation": "What is the matter?"}, {"id": "de-quote36", "translation": "What epitaph—?"}, {"id": "de-quote37", "translation": "Mother of the king, and my queen."}, {"id": "de-quote38", "translation": "My husband, and a corpse."}, {"id": "de-quote39", "translation": "A faithful wife, but worn by the benches of sailors."}, {"id": "de-quote40", "translation": "The mother of the child called hers, but nurse of the newly sown wave,"}, {"id": "de-quote41", "translation": "Alas, you gods! Alas, for the avengers—."}, {"id": "de-quote42", "translation": "AN. To say double things. IS. To see double things."}, {"id": "de-quote43", "translation": "Free your country, free—."}, {"id": "de-quote44", "translation": "He was called god-counselled by the Persians, and god-counselled he was."}, {"id": "de-quote45", "translation": "The toil is past, and past—."}, {"id": "de-quote46", "translation": "A king without citizens, and without mourning."}, {"id": "de-quote47", "translation": "Terrible to say, and terrible to see with the eyes."}, {"id": "de-quote48", "translation": "Zeus is the air, Zeus is the earth, Zeus is the sky."}, {"id": "de-quote49", "translation": "But if you do not understand and do not accept my words, then instead of speech, make signs with your barbarian hand."}, {"id": "de-quote50", "translation": "But if the holy majesty of Persuasion is dear to you, then you may remain."}, {"id": "de-quote51", "translation": "But when I remembered the relentless toils, and untimely—."}, {"id": "de-quote52", "translation": "But when the crowd of ships was gathered in the narrow strait, and no help was at hand for one another, and they themselves were struck by their own bronze-beaked rams—,"}, {"id": "de-quote53", "translation": "I agree—but how is it possible to disobey the words of a father?"}, {"id": "de-quote54", "translation": "But the boast."}, {"id": "de-quote55", "translation": "But your people."}, {"id": "de-quote56", "translation": "But the destined one."}, {"id": "de-quote57", "translation": "But the divided one."}, {"id": "de-quote58", "translation": "But the rest."}, {"id": "de-quote59", "translation": "But the former things."}, {"id": "de-quote60", "translation": "But I, double."}, {"id": "de-quote61", "translation": "Hephaestus, you must attend to the commands,"}, {"id": "de-quote62", "translation": "O Persephassa, grant fair victory."}, {"id": "de-quote63", "translation": "I myself am an eyewitness of the events."}, {"id": "de-quote64", "translation": "But of the long journey."}, {"id": "de-quote65", "translation": "But of the ancestral rites."}, {"id": "de-quote66", "translation": "But with many present."}, {"id": "de-quote67", "translation": "But in what way?"}, {"id": "de-quote68", "translation": "But by what fate?"}, {"id": "de-quote69", "translation": "But of what time?"}, {"id": "de-quote70", "translation": "But a blazing torch."}, {"id": "de-quote71", "translation": "But a faithful wife."}, {"id": "de-quote72", "translation": "But of the ancestral altar."}, {"id": "de-quote73", "translation": "But of prudent judgment."}, {"id": "de-quote74", "translation": "But a new report,"}, {"id": "de-quote75", "translation": "But Pallas Pronaia."}, {"id": "de-quote76", "translation": "But being a suppliant."}, {"id": "de-quote77", "translation": "But being a prophet."}, {"id": "de-quote78", "translation": "But a stoner of the people."}, {"id": "de-quote79", "translation": "But heaps of corpses."}, {"id": "de-quote80", "translation": "But struck by misfortunes, wandering far."}, {"id": "de-quote81", "translation": "But to this very thing."}, {"id": "de-quote82", "translation": "But from a man."}, {"id": "de-quote83", "translation": "But not a coward."}, {"id": "de-quote84", "translation": "But thus utterly."}, {"id": "de-quote85", "translation": "But whenever."}, {"id": "de-quote86", "translation": "But if all things."}, {"id": "de-quote87", "translation": "But not so as to help,"}, {"id": "de-quote88", "translation": "But one to one place, another to another."}, {"id": "de-quote89", "translation": "But before dying."}, {"id": "de-quote90", "translation": "But to be without honor."}, {"id": "de-quote91", "translation": "But turning aside, she accomplished."}, {"id": "de-quote92", "translation": "But I am a guest-friend in these matters."}, {"id": "de-quote93", "translation": "But having fallen asleep."}, {"id": "de-quote94", "translation": "But I declare by counsel."}, {"id": "de-quote95", "translation": "But in addition to the present circumstances."}, {"id": "de-quote96", "translation": "But in forethought."}, {"id": "de-quote97", "translation": "But the things for mortals."}, {"id": "de-quote98", "translation": "But the things from outside."}, {"id": "de-quote99", "translation": "But if the gods are willing, I would speak the truth."}, {"id": "de-quote100", "translation": "But from those in power."}, {"id": "de-quote101", "translation": "But in every matter."}, {"id": "de-quote102", "translation": "But on foot or as a sailor."}, {"id": "de-quote103", "translation": "But being mortal, of the gods."}, {"id": "de-quote104", "translation": "But in the night, storm-tossed."}, {"id": "de-quote105", "translation": "But for the whole."}, {"id": "de-quote106", "translation": "But not to delay."}, {"id": "de-quote107", "translation": "But the things of the father."}, {"id": "de-quote108", "translation": "But not vain."}, {"id": "de-quote109", "translation": "But not to have been born."}, {"id": "de-quote110", "translation": "But shedding a tear-stained stream from my tender eyes, I wet my cheek with moist drops,"}, {"id": "de-quote111", "translation": "But Justice says it is."}, {"id": "de-quote112", "translation": "But from righteous houses, a fate with fair children always,"}, {"id": "de-quote113", "translation": "But I, the men—."}, {"id": "de-quote114", "translation": "But what else—."}, {"id": "de-quote115", "translation": "But the unenvied man is not enviable."}, {"id": "de-quote116", "translation": "But for the prosperous."}, {"id": "de-quote117", "translation": "But the toil of a man nourishes two days."}, {"id": "de-quote118", "translation": "O Persephassa, grant fair victory."}, {"id": "de-quote119", "translation": "But they will find many in the heat of midday."}]}